{{!-- The ready-to-paste client configuration, lifted out of mcp-default.hbs's old
      col-lg-5 into the page's right rail, where upstream keeps it.

      Two departures from upstream, both deliberate:
      - the copy button reuses copyToken(this, id) rather than a bespoke copyMcpConfig.
        copyToken already drives this exact .copy-btn markup elsewhere on the page and
        reads #token_<id>, so naming the <pre> token_mcp_config needs no new script. The
        old copyServerConfig relied on the button being the <pre>'s nextElementSibling,
        which stops being true once the button is absolutely positioned inside the block.
      - upstream nests its subscription plans inside this panel. Ours stay a sibling in
        the rail so the MCP page shows the same plan card as the API page. --}}
<div class="mc-config-panel">
  <h2 class="aov-section-title mc-config-title">MCP Server Configuration</h2>
  <div class="mc-config-block">
    <button type="button" class="copy-btn mc-config-copy" title="Copy configuration"
      onclick="copyToken(this, 'mcp_config')">
      <span class="copy-btn-icon"><i class="bi bi-copy"></i></span>
      <span class="copy-btn-check"><i class="bi bi-check"></i> Copied</span>
    </button>
    {{!-- One line on purpose. Handlebars prepends this partial's own call indentation
          (12 spaces, page.hbs) to every template line, and <pre> preserves it - written
          out as literal JSON lines here, the block rendered ragged in the browser however
          neatly it was nested in the source. An interpolated value is not re-indented, so
          the helper returns the whole block already formatted. --}}
    <pre id="token_mcp_config" class="mc-config-pre"><code class="language-json">{{{mcpServerConfig apiMetadata.apiInfo.apiName resources.serverDetails.productionURL}}}</code></pre>
  </div>
  <p class="mc-config-note">Generate a token using a subscribed application and replace the placeholder.</p>
</div>
